                <pb facs="0387" n="255" xml:id="pg255"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.415C/–: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >South</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-04-24T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 24,
                                1926—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>33. Your despatch No. 678, April 2, 1925. Department assumes congress to which
                    invitation refers will be of a purely ceremonial and commemorative nature and
                    that no discussion of international matters is contemplated. Discreetly verify
                    and report by cable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
